---
title: "Company setup: conventions"
description: Chart of accounts, contacts, rules, fixed assets, policies and memory.
sidebar:
  order: 6
  label: "Setup: conventions"
---

These tabs of **Company setup** hold how this company's books are kept. Every item here applies to all periods of the company. **Chart of Accounts**, **Contacts** and **Fixed Assets** are in the **Company profile** group; **Policies**, **Rules** and **Memory** are in the **Bookkeeping conventions** group.

| Tab | Group | What it holds |
|---|---|---|
| **Chart of Accounts** | Company profile | The company's accounts. Add, rename or retire an account here. |
| **Contacts** | Company profile | Suppliers and customers, with the names under which they appear on bank statements and invoices. |
| **Rules** | Bookkeeping conventions | The account mapping: which account and tax code a kind of transaction is booked to. A rule can come from the firm's defaults, from prior years or from a person. |
| **Fixed Assets** | Company profile | The fixed asset register: cost, date, useful life and depreciation. |
| **Policies** | Bookkeeping conventions | The period-end rules: accruals, prepayments, depreciation, foreign-currency revaluation and similar items. |
| **Memory** | Bookkeeping conventions | What Operon has learned from the decisions made for this company. |

{% screenshot id="bookkeeping/setup-conventions-rules" caption="The Rules tab, with a rule for bank charges." /%}

## Suggestions and confirmation

Operon suggests account mappings, rules and policies from prior years' books and from the decisions made in earlier periods. A suggestion takes effect only once a person confirms it.

{% aside type="tip" %}
Keep the conventions current. A wrong rule is repeated on every later document; correcting it early saves corrections later.
{% /aside %}
